From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000246 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 13:50:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: add source-backed MT6797 SB0119 table family

Add a pure source-backed table-family reader for the MT6797 SB/0119
frequency arrays identified in the public Gemini kernel and matched by a
read-only probe on the named device. The reader requires the decoded PTP
date identity and rejects other date families; it returns the three physical
cluster arrays, the separate CCI array, and a stable source epoch.

This is deliberately not a PPM owner: it does not claim the vendor PPM lock,
active policy limits, mutable table generation, calibration handle, clock or
rail state, or a transition owner. KUnit coverage proves the exact arrays and
fail-closed identity check without a platform probe or hardware access. This
patch is experiment-only and not submission-ready.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/Makefile                         |   2 +
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-table-source-test.c | 102 ++++++++++++
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-table-source.c      | 109 +++++++++++++
 include/linux/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-table-source.h |  35 ++++
 4 files changed, 248 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-table-source-test.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-table-source.c
 create mode 100644 include/linux/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-table-source.h

